# Code owners. feature-loop stages 6 and 7 both gate on "a human code owner approved" — this
# file is what makes GitHub able to enforce that instead of trusting it.
#
# An unknown handle here is IGNORED SILENTLY by GitHub, which turns the gate back off without
# telling anyone. When someone joins or leaves, change this file in the same PR.
#
# Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection for `main`, or this file only
# requests reviewers rather than requiring them.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @your-org/mobile-reviewers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- steers every session
# The skills, hooks and agents decide how every future change gets built. A quiet edit here is
# far more expensive than a quiet edit to a screen.
/.claude/                @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/AGENTS.md               @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/REVIEW.md               @your-org/mobile-reviewers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- release and security
# Version policy, signing, store submission, and the scanners. A mistake here is a rejected
# submission, an OTA update on a binary that cannot run it, or a leaked credential.
/eas.json                @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/.eas/                   @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/app.json                @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/store.config.json       @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/.github/workflows/      @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/.semgrep.yml            @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/.gitleaks.toml          @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/.zap/                   @your-org/mobile-reviewers
/commitlint.config.js    @your-org/mobile-reviewers
